      <article class="toc-content prose">
    <p style="padding:1.25rem;background:var(--bg-alt);border-left:3px solid var(--gold-500);border-radius:0 var(--radius-sm) var(--radius-sm) 0;margin-bottom:2rem"><strong>Reference copy.</strong> This is the template, not a contract you sign here. You sign your own copy from the sign-up page.</p>

    <h2 id="parties">1. The parties</h2>
    <p>This agreement is between <strong>Pikes Peak Web Designs</strong>, a Colorado sole proprietorship operated by Jon Ajinga (referred to as "Pikes Peak" or "I"), and the <strong>Client</strong> (you), an individual or business entity engaging me to design, build, and maintain a website.</p>

    <h2 id="scope">2. Scope of services</h2>
    <p>Under the standard plan, I agree to provide the following:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Custom-coded website design and development covering up to ten content pages</li>
      <li>Eight operational pages included at no cost and outside the ten-page count: Privacy Policy, Accessibility Statement, Terms of Use, Contact page, Thank-You page, Testimonials page, Style Guide, and Sitemap</li>
      <li>Standard build features: light and dark mode with system-preference detection, responsive header and navigation, an accessible mobile hamburger menu, built-in Pagefind search, privacy-focused analytics, WCAG 2.2 AA accessibility, and CDN-served performance</li>
      <li>The blog system, included, with a paginated index, post template, sticky table of contents, reading-progress bar, share buttons, RSS feed, and BlogPosting JSON-LD schema</li>
      <li>Technical infrastructure files: robots.txt, humans.txt, security.txt, sitemap.xml, RSS feed, 404 page, favicon suite, and Open Graph / Twitter images</li>
      <li>Website hosting on a fast global CDN with SSL</li>
      <li>Unlimited content updates during the term of the agreement</li>
      <li>Direct emergency support for site-down or site-critical issues</li>
      <li>On-page and local SEO foundation (meta, schema, sitemap, structured headings, NAP consistency)</li>
      <li>Ongoing security monitoring and maintenance</li>
    </ul>
    <h2 id="fees">3. Fees and payment</h2>
    <p><strong>Monthly Plan:</strong> $175 USD per month, billed on a consistent monthly cycle, with a 12-month minimum term. After the first 12 months, the agreement converts to month-to-month with 30 days' written notice to cancel.</p>
    <p><strong>Additional pages:</strong> $100 USD for each content page beyond the ten included.</p>
    <p><strong>Refunds:</strong> if you cancel before I begin work on your site, I refund your first payment in full. Once work has begun, payments already made are not refundable.</p>
    <p><strong>Hourly work outside the standard plan:</strong> $100 USD per hour. The standard plan covers the design, build, hosting, security, blog, on-page and local SEO foundation, and unlimited content updates within the scope of your site. Moving content from an existing website is part of the build at no extra cost. Anything outside that scope, such as custom-built calculators, third-party booking integrations, or email-marketing templates, is billed hourly with a written estimate provided before any work begins.</p>
    <p>All prices exclude applicable sales tax. Payments are processed through <a href="https://stripe.com" rel="noopener" class="inline-link">Stripe</a>, which handles the card or ACH transaction directly. I never see or store your card number on my end of the wire, since Stripe holds all payment information on their PCI-compliant infrastructure and only sends me a confirmation that the charge cleared.</p>

    <h2 id="timeline">4. Timeline</h2>
    <p>Work begins when your first payment clears. My target is to design, build, and launch your site within two to three weeks of that date, provided you can deliver basic content (logo, photos, and a list of services) in the first week. I commit to doing my part. I'm not responsible for delays caused by late content or approvals, but I'll keep you informed either way.</p>

    <h2 id="your-responsibilities">5. Your responsibilities</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Provide accurate, honest information about your business</li>
      <li>Review and approve designs within a reasonable timeframe</li>
      <li>Keep your account current and respond to payment issues promptly</li>
      <li>Do not ask me to build anything illegal, defamatory, or infringing</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="my-responsibilities">6. My responsibilities</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Deliver a custom-coded, accessible, fast website fit for your business</li>
      <li>Handle hosting, security, and maintenance (Monthly Plan) without extra billing</li>
      <li>Reply quickly to content-update requests on most business days</li>
      <li>Treat emergencies as queue-jumping work and handle them fast on most business days</li>
      <li>Tell you, in plain language, when something is outside scope or unreasonable</li>
      <li>Be the same person who takes your call, writes your code, and makes your updates, with no queue and no hand-off</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="ownership">7. Ownership</h2>
    <p>I own the source code and host it on your behalf while the agreement is active. Your domain is always registered in your name and never mine, and your photos, text, and brand assets remain yours throughout the engagement.</p>

    <h2 id="cancellation">8. Cancellation</h2>
    <p>After the 12-month minimum, either party may cancel with 30 days' written notice. Within the 12-month minimum, early cancellation by the Client requires payment of the remaining monthly installments under the agreement. I will not cancel on you without cause unless you materially violate these terms.</p>
    <p>At cancellation, I'll help you move your domain to a registrar of your choice. The website goes offline at the end of the term. I don't provide a copy or export of the website's code or files.</p>

    <h2 id="confidentiality">9. Confidentiality</h2>
    <p>Anything you share with me in confidence stays in confidence: business strategy, pricing, internal documents, customer data. I will not share your information with third parties except as required to deliver the services (e.g. your domain registrar, the hosting provider) or as required by law.</p>

    <h2 id="warranties">10. Warranties and limitation of liability</h2>
    <p>I warrant that the work will be performed professionally and that the deliverables will be free of my negligent errors at the time of launch. I do not guarantee any particular search ranking, sales outcome, or business result; I guarantee my workmanship and my responsiveness.</p>
    <p>My total liability under this agreement is limited to the fees you have paid in the 12 months preceding any claim.</p>

    <h2 id="governing-law">11. Governing law</h2>
    <p>This agreement is governed by the laws of the State of Colorado, United States. Disputes will be resolved first through friendly discussion, then through mediation, and finally (if needed) in the state and federal courts located in El Paso County, Colorado.</p>

    <h2 id="signatures">12. Signatures</h2>
    <p>The copy you sign has signature blocks for both parties, dates, and your business details. You sign it in Documenso, an e-signature service, from the sign-up page. It takes about two minutes on a phone or laptop, with no printing, scanning, or faxing.</p>

    <hr>

    <p style="font-size:0.9rem;color:var(--text-muted)">Questions about this agreement? <a href="/contact/" class="inline-link">Get in touch</a>. I'd rather answer questions now than have surprises later.</p>

